A||N||14||loafer87gt||My bad experience with GM... ||||11||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||04-02-2000||11:30 PM||||I got my GT back from the GM dealership a couple of days ago. I took it there because the car will randomly stall and the revs will surge between stalling and normal revs (it is like you are stomping on and off the gas pedal) I have now had it back to them four times trying to figure out what is causing the problem, and the this time they told me it appears to be a dead ECM. Anyways, I told them I wanted them to save my old ECM from my car so that I had proof that they actually changed the part, but I was told that they have to automatically send the old damaged ECM back to GM because they rebuild them, so they wouldn't show me the old module. Well, my car died on the way home and the same problem is still there. I don't know what to do, they are the only GM dealership in town that said they will work on my car, and my car came new from them back in 87. They have still not been able to find the problem on my car, they have replaced the plugs, plug wires, ignition module, coil, distributor, done several diagnostics, and recently replaced my computer and the car still won't run. I am considering taking legal action,I have now spent over $1300 trying to fix the problem, and they won't refund or take back any of the parts that they have installed trying to get the car fixed. Add to this over $200 in towing charges, that they won't even cover! The two things they haven't replaced yet that have been showing up in the engine diagnostic are the MAP sensor and the EGR valve is not working properly, but they said this wouldn't cause the problem. I just don't know what to do, no GM dealership besides this place will work on my car because its a Fiero, and I don't want to go to another place to start right from square one again. I don't know how to go about trying to recoupe some of the money I have dumped into my car. Does anyone know of a GM customer satisfaction phone number or anything that I could phone and file a complaint to? ||||reg||11
Z||000001||Oreif||04-03-2000||12:18 AM||||The best way to get the problem solved or corrected is call the dealer in the morning and ask them for the phone number for the GM zone representative. These are the people who can authorize repairs or refunds. They work for GM not the dealer. It is there job to keep the dealers in line since they are representing GM. I know a few people who have had problems with various types of GM cars and the dealers did not want to cooperate. Once the zone office gets involved the dealer becomes a lot more "enthusiastic" in correcting the problem. Especially if you have taken the car to the same dealer for the same problem.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||04-03-2000||02:15 AM||||For God's sake, STOP TAKING IT TO THE DEALER!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Earne||04-03-2000||07:37 AM||||loafer87gt,<P>What Orief told you works.  All manufacturers have these reps.  My sister bought a minivan from a local Ford dealer.  They tried to tell her that it was usual for a new car to burn a quart of oil per month.  The Ford rep looked into her problem and found a history of complaints with the dealership.  She ended up with a new engine, no charge, loaner.  <P>The point is, manufacturer competition is very stiff these days and they are not fond of most of their dealers (read middleman).  With the increased use of the internet, mnfr's plan to eliminate many dealers in favor of service centers.  Those dealerships with poor service records are on the endangered list.  Contact the area rep, be insistent, they will listen and take action.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DJRice||04-03-2000||11:26 AM||||Please tell me they replaced the tach filter already!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||loafer87gt||04-03-2000||12:29 PM||||Nope, its not the tach filter, the problem is really hard to describe. Its not like it is a suttle tach fluctuation, it is like you mashing on and off the gas pedal, almost like when you are learning to drive a stick and pop the clutch to early. The jerkiness is bad enough that one of my passengers banged his head off the dash when it started to do it on the way home last weekend. I don't know if the problem is moisture related, because out of the four times the car has died on me, one time was after washing the car, and once was during a snowstorm.I talked to the guys again this morning and the best they are going to do for me is pay half of my towing bill to get it back to them, as my car is stuck up in the middle of nowhere in Northern Canada. So, I'm going to call the Zone Rep right now and see what they can do for me, frankly, I'm not expecting anything. GM has let me down every time I have dealt with them, and I swear I will never buy another GM vehicle as long as I live. They seem to not have any loyalty to their customer or to their vehicles. When was the last time you went to a Toyota dealership and hear them badmouth one of their vehicles? But last summer I went to Mann Motors GM dealership to get my "100 K of Pontiac Excitement" plate and was told that the Fiero is car that Pontiac is still trying to forget about. Comments like these hurt the customer, and in the end, make them look incompetent. Anyways, I have a list of all the comments, problems, that I have dealt with at GM dealerships, and I am going to put it forward to them and give them my point of view on their service. Wish me luck...||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||04-03-2000||07:35 PM||||you ran it w/o the tach filter to make sure?||||reg||1
Z||000007||loafer87gt||04-03-2000||07:54 PM||||I replaced the tach filter last fall, so I don't think its the culprit. Besides, when my tach filter went my tach acted up, but the car still ran great. Whatever is causing this problem is something electrical or computer related I'm pretty sure. The problem is really hard to describe, it doesn't matter what revs you are at, the car will run at the right rev, then cut out, run at the right revs, cut. It does this for about 1/2 intervals. When you hold the gas down it goes BLAT!, BLAT!, BLAT!, BLAT!, or if you take your foot off the gas, the car just stalls and dies. Very tough to describe the problem in words. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Richard Parnell||04-03-2000||08:14 PM||||Have you checked that the catalytic converter is not plugged?||||reg||5
Z||000009||loafer87gt||04-03-2000||08:45 PM||||I removed the catalytic convertor when I did the exhaust system on my car, so nope, not the prob. Thanks you all for your ideas though||||reg||1
Z||000010||sdm1964||04-03-2000||09:45 PM||||sorry to hear sbout you bad fortune, but did you check the IAC, idle air controler? just a quick thought||||reg||13
Z||000011||fieroshop||04-03-2000||09:48 PM||||Well experience tells me that if at idle the engine surges then you may have a map sensor problem. Get yourself another sensor and try that. That is the only thing that I can figure from what you wrote.||||reg||8
Z||000012||fierospeeder||04-03-2000||09:52 PM||||Did you ask them to change your ECM again?  <BR>I read some stories on some of the remanufactured ECMs were still bad.<P>I know some of the GM dealers are d*cks <BR>My moms car 2.8 celebrity wagon was stalling and wasn't running right.  They changed the prom with an updated one for the mass air flow sensor.  Im thinking logically, has the air changed that much since 10 years ago.  The car later acted the same.  Later found out the Ignition module was going bad.  Put in a new one for 100 bucks. "Did it my self"||||reg||1
Z||000013||Racer 1||04-03-2000||10:26 PM||||Sorry to hear about your bad experience with your dealer.<P>I had almost the same problem on my fiero but mines a 4 banger. My distributor shaft that goes down in your engine had crud on it and everytime the engine would heat up it would stall and then act wierd. I replaced the whole distibutor assembly and it fixed it. Also check your little black ignition module inside your distibutor cap that causes problems to when it goes bad. If thats bad get one directly from GM. Check your ECM and see what codes are popping up. Good Luck <P>My GM dealer is cool. One time I ordered some buttons that hold on the front fenders "the big black ones" and he told me to stick them in my pocket and go "FREE". <P>One more thing does your check engine light stay on?<p>[This message has been edited by Racer 1 (edited 04-03-2000).]||||reg||12
Z||000014||007DOUG||04-05-2000||12:32 AM||||Sounds like the coolant temp sensor. <P>the sensor is telling the computer its cold, and feeding it a ton of gas (is your gas mileage bad too?) When you stop, it floods and stalls.<P>Is it difficult to get restarted when warm?<P>When warm, is the computer in the correct loop? <P>Does the car run fine when cold?<P>Maybe replace the temp sensor. Make sure you replace the right one...NOT the fan/gauge temp sensor.<P>I had the similar problems with my fiero and a temp sensor (for the computer) was the problem.<P>Doug<BR>||||reg||1
